          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><h3>Annotation</h3><table class=\"hl7__eu__lab__report\"><tr><th>Conclusion and Recommendations based on this report and previous findings known to us:</th></tr><tr><td>The patient shows a mildly to moderately decreased glomerular filtration rate (GFR) at 39 mL/min/1.73m², below the normal range, indicating stage 3b chronic kidney disease. This suggests impaired renal function, which is not uncommon in elderly patients. Clinical correlation and monitoring of renal function, as well as assessment for potential underlying causes or complications, are recommended.</td></tr></table></div>"
